---
import BaseLayout from '@shared/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import AdSense from '@shared/components/AdSense.astro';

const title = 'kdp.cool — Free, fast, no-signup web tools';
const description = 'Kdp.Cool builds focused single-purpose web tools for everyday tasks: financial calculators, format converters, developer utilities, and writing helpers. Free, fast, ad-supported.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} pathname="/" schemaType="WebSite">
  <section class="grid items-center gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1.05fr_0.95fr]">
    <div class="max-w-4xl">
      <p class="kdp-section-label mb-4">A small public toolbox, maintained by hand</p>
      <h1 class="text-5xl font-semibold leading-[0.98] sm:text-6xl lg:text-7xl">Free web tools that actually feel fast</h1>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-8 text-stone-700">
        No signups, no popups, no dark patterns. Each tool runs in your browser, returns results instantly, and shows the math behind the answer. We pay the bills with non-intrusive ads — that's the whole deal.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="relative">
      <div class="absolute -inset-4 rounded-[2rem] bg-[#f3eadc]/70 blur-2xl" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <img
        src="/toolbench.svg"
        alt="A warm editorial illustration of calculator, converter, text, developer, and AI utility panels"
        width="960"
        height="640"
        class="relative w-full rounded-[1.75rem] border border-[#e6d9c8] bg-white shadow-[0_20px_60px_rgba(92,64,36,0.14)]"
      />
    </figure>
  </section>

  <AdSense adSlot="portal-top" style="min-height:90px" />

  <section class="mt-10">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-2 sm:flex-row sm:items-end sm:justify-between">
      <div>
        <p class="kdp-section-label">On this site</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 font-serif text-3xl font-semibold tracking-normal text-stone-950">Calculators you can use here</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="max-w-md text-sm leading-6 text-stone-600">These three run on kdp.cool. Each page shows the formula, the sources, and what the result does not include.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 mt-6 sm:grid-cols-3">
      <a href="/mortgage-calculator/" class="kdp-card block rounded-2xl p-5 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-teal-700 focus-visible:ring-offset-2">
        <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold tracking-normal">Mortgage</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-stone-600">Monthly principal and interest, plus a simple tax and insurance draft. The $400,000 example is also written out below.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/paycheck-calculator/" class="kdp-card block rounded-2xl p-5 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-teal-700 focus-visible:ring-offset-2">
        <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold tracking-normal">Paycheck</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-stone-600">Federal brackets, FICA, an optional flat state rate, and pretax deductions, split across pay periods.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/income-tax-calculator/" class="kdp-card block rounded-2xl p-5 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-teal-700 focus-visible:ring-offset-2">
        <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold tracking-normal">Federal income tax</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-stone-600">2026 ordinary brackets from IRS Revenue Procedure 2025-32, stacked one band at a time.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm">
      <a href="/guides/" class="kdp-link">Read the worked guides</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-14 border-t border-[#e6d9c8] pt-8">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-2 sm:flex-row sm:items-end sm:justify-between">
      <div>
        <p class="kdp-section-label">Static math, no JavaScript required</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 font-serif text-3xl font-semibold tracking-normal text-stone-950">Worked examples</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="max-w-md text-sm leading-6 text-stone-600">Two short cases you can check with a calculator. The longer write-ups live in <a href="/guides/" class="kdp-link">Guides</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <article class="kdp-card rounded-2xl p-5">
        <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold tracking-normal">$400,000 mortgage</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-stone-600">20% down, 6.5% annual rate, 30 years. Principal is $320,000. The standard amortizing formula gives monthly principal and interest of <strong>$2,022.62</strong>. Add $5,000/year property tax ($416.67) and $1,500/year insurance ($125) and the housing draft is <strong>$2,564.28</strong>.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-stone-600">Month 1 interest is $320,000 × 0.065 / 12 = $1,733.33, so only $289.28 goes to principal. That split is why early payments feel interest-heavy.</p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm">
          <a href="/guides/how-monthly-mortgage-payments-are-calculated/" class="kdp-link">Read the mortgage guide -&gt;</a>
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="kdp-card rounded-2xl p-5">
        <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold tracking-normal">$72,000 paycheck</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-stone-600">Single filer, biweekly, no state income tax, no 401(k), tax year 2026. Taxable income is $72,000 − $16,100 = $55,900. Federal tax stacks as $1,240 + $4,560 + $1,210 = <strong>$7,010</strong>. FICA adds $4,464 Social Security and $1,044 Medicare.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-stone-600">Estimated take-home is <strong>$59,482</strong> a year, or about <strong>$2,287.77</strong> every other week — closer to 17% combined federal-plus-FICA than to a flat 22%.</p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm">
          <a href="/guides/how-to-read-take-home-pay/" class="kdp-link">Read the paycheck guide -&gt;</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="kdp-prose mt-14 max-w-3xl border-t border-[#e6d9c8] pt-8">
    <p class="kdp-section-label mb-2">Scope</p>
    <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-semibold tracking-normal text-stone-950">When to use these tools — and when not to</h2>
    <div class="mt-5 grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-stone-950">When to use them</h3>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
          <li>You want a ballpark payment, tax, or conversion before you talk to a lender, payroll office, or accountant.</li>
          <li>You want to see the formula or the bracket stack, not just a final number.</li>
          <li>You want to share a scenario via the URL without creating an account.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-stone-950">When not to</h3>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
          <li>Do not treat a calculator result as a loan offer, a filed tax return, or legal advice.</li>
          <li>Do not skip official documents: Loan Estimates, W-2s, Publication 15-T, or Form 1040 instructions.</li>
          <li>Do not enter secrets, customer data, or tax documents. The tools are for numbers you are comfortable typing in a browser.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-6">
      For the longer versions of the two examples above, plus guides on term tradeoffs, prepayments, FICA versus ordinary tax, 401(k) deferrals, and marginal versus effective rates, start at <a href="/guides/" class="kdp-link">kdp.cool/guides</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="kdp-prose mt-14 max-w-3xl border-t border-[#e6d9c8] pt-8">
    <p class="kdp-section-label mb-2">Editorial rules</p>
    <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-semibold tracking-normal text-stone-950">Why kdp.cool</h2>
    <ul class="mt-5 space-y-3 list-disc pl-6">
      <li><strong>Speed and clarity first.</strong> Tools render in under a second and recalculate as you type. No loading spinners on basic math.</li>
      <li><strong>No email walls.</strong> We don't gate features behind signups, "premium" tiers, or "free trial" funnels. Everything is free, forever.</li>
      <li><strong>Show the math.</strong> Our calculators include a "Show the math" toggle that reveals the formula and intermediate steps. You can verify the answer or learn the method.</li>
      <li><strong>Corrections in public.</strong> If a figure is wrong, email <a href="mailto:hello@kdp.cool" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">hello@kdp.cool</a> with the page URL and the numbers you expected.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <AdSense adSlot="portal-bottom" style="min-height:90px" />

  <section class="mt-12 border-t border-[#e6d9c8] pt-6 text-sm text-stone-600">
    <p class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-2">
      <a href="/guides/" class="hover:text-stone-950">Guides</a>
      <a href="/about/" class="hover:text-stone-950">About</a>
      <a href="/privacy/" class="hover:text-stone-950">Privacy</a>
      <a href="/terms/" class="hover:text-stone-950">Terms</a>
      <a href="/contact/" class="hover:text-stone-950">Contact</a>
      <a href="mailto:hello@kdp.cool" class="hover:text-stone-950">Email</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
